{"title":"2019 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Ali plays a trivia game with 5 categories, each with 3 questions. She earns 1 point for each correct answer. If she answers all 3 questions in a category correctly, she earns 1 bonus point. Ali answers exactly 12 questions correctly and the remaining 3 questions incorrectly. What are her possible total scores?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can split the problem into different cases based on the distribution of the incorrect answers: having all three incorrect answers be in a single category (meaning four categories have , having one category have two incorrect answers and one have one incorrect answer while all other categories having all correct answers (three categories), and having three categories have one incorrect answer each but the other two categories have all correct answers. We also automatically know that since she had <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> points automatically since she had <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> correct answers.\n</p><p>If Ali has all correct answers in four categories but all incorrect answers in the fifth category, then she must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> extra points for the categories that she had all correct answers in, so she would have a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/2/ff25856946ba8a80bbeb39f213abb6ccded50342.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 + 4 = \\boxed{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"105\" height=\"25\" /> points.\n</p><p>If Ali has one category with two incorrect answers, one with one incorrect answer, and three categories with correct answers, then she must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> extra points for the categories that she had all correct answers in, so she would have a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/6/2268fbc4f09d045dbb0b6ef2267d92e01cd88b0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 + 3 = \\boxed{15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"105\" height=\"25\" /> points.\n</p><p>If Ali has three categories each with one incorrect answer with two categories with all correct answers, then she must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> extra points for the categories that she had all correct answers in, so she would have a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/5/0850e5a861da69ccf0aeb9c9a98bf6afa296dbbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 + 2 = \\boxed{14}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"105\" height=\"25\" /> points.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIMC\" title=\"2019 CIMC\">2019 CIMC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIMC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2019 CIMC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIMC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2019 CIMC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_3\" title=\"2019 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 3\">Part A Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2019 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Part A Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_1\" title=\"2019 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 1\">Part A 1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2\" title=\"2019 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 2\">Part A 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_3\" title=\"2019 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 3\">Part A 3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Part A 4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2019 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Part A 5</a> <b>•</